  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "the physical cause of the positioner failure was a combination of high cycle fatigue of the positioner associated with positioner movement demand and the presence of impurities in the instrument air supply to the positioner. The failure of the backup positioner to assume control was attributed to a latent design error during implementation of the modification that installed the positioners, which resulted in the inability of the positioner swapover function to detect an internal failure of the primary positioner.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
